A photorealistic scene of cardboard moving boxes stacked haphazardly in an empty room with warm afternoon sunlight streaming through bare windows, casting long dramatic shadows across polished wooden floors. In the foreground, a single worn suitcase sits open, revealing glimpses of carefully folded fabric. Dust particles float visibly in the golden light beams. The walls show faint rectangular outlines where picture frames once hung. Through the window, tropical palm trees and Singapore's distinctive HDB apartment blocks are visible in the soft-focus background. The atmosphere conveys both endings and beginnings, nostalgia mixed with anticipation.
